1.3 What is inside the log file?

if log_path is not None and log_path.exists():
    print("--- first line of the log ---")
    print(log_path.read_text().splitlines()[0])
else:
    print("No file handler active; the log only goes to stdout.")

--- first line of the log ---
{"schema_version":"1.0.0","timestamp_utc":"2026-05-31T19:50:53.303584Z","logger":"task_safe_n_to_1","level":"INFO","event":"audit_log_init","message":"Persistent logging initialized at: _cache/logs/task_safe_n_to_1_20260531_215053.log"}


Every entry contains timestamp, logger name, level (INFO/WARNING/ERROR/DEBUG) and text. These four fields are enough for a later auditor to reconstruct the exact order and content of every action.
